{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation note — test placement deviates from the recorded file_impact.\n\nThe three queue-bound tests (per-type open count, pre-enqueue CLAIM skip, corrupt-newest fallback) landed in tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py, not tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py as file_impact declared. test_enrich_queue.py is the cohesive home for llm/overlap/queue.py — it already owns the enqueue/soak/claim/lease/reduce suite and the fixtures these tests need. test_enrich_drain.py covers the drain-gate wiring and is unchanged; it is still run as a regression (passes).\n\nThe AC4 filename/body-timestamp coupling test landed in tests/unit/test_store.py as declared, next to the canonical-bytes tests, asserting on the real stage_and_commit output rather than re-deriving the name via event_filename.\n\nRED verified: against the pre-change queue.py the two bound tests fail — reduce opened 90 queue files (now <= 3) and claim arbitration read 40 stale pre-enqueue CLAIM files (now <= 1, which is reduce_ticket's own newest-CLAIM probe).\n\nAlso added test_all_events_corrupt_reads_as_absent, pinning the terminal case of the newest-first walk (every matching file unparseable -> the type reduces as absent) — the gap the plan review raised as a dropped advisory."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786501422002651001,"uuid":"7a7ae71e-96a2-4eff-8d5c-dd88c5b817aa"}